    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="IRS990ScheduleO1" documentName="IRS990ScheduleO">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part VI, Line 7a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Part VI Line 7a: Each Supervisor on the County of San Diego Board of Supervisors has the power to elect or appoint one member of the SANCAL Board of Directors for a total of 5 Directors.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part VI, Line 7b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Part VI Line 7b: SANCAL is an independent advisory board appointed by the County Board of Supervisors and reports directly to the Board of Supervisors. The activities and affairs of SANCAL are subject to the approval of the County Board of Supervisors.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part VI, Line 8a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Part VI Line 8b: SANCAL does not have any committees.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part VI, Line 11a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Part VI Line 11a,b: SANCAL does not have a formal process to review Form 990. The form is prepared and reviewed by County of San Diego fiscal staff. A final review and all signatures are provided by the principal officer of SANCAL.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part VI, Line 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Part IV Lines 12a b c and 19: SANCALs governing documents Conflict of Interest Code and the county of San Diegos Annual Comprehensive Financial Report ACFR which includes the financial reports of SANCAL are available upon request. Additional The Conflict of Interest Code is located at https: www.sandiegocounty.gov content dam sdc cob docs conflict_interest SANCAL.pdf The audited financial statements ACFR are located at https: www.sandiegocounty.gov auditor cafr.html</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part XII Line 1</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>| Explanation:| Part XII line 1: The County of San Diego uses the modified accrual method of accounting for SANCAL. This combines accrual-basis accounting with cash basis accounting.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleO>
